course: dictionary
lesson: 2993
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and dummy is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues. Then ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Crash-test dummies full of sensors ride in new cars that are crashed on purpose.» The words crashed and sensors are the clues. Here a dummy is a model of a person, used to test how safe a car is.
explain: «Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers and compared with a dummy pill.» The clues are tested, compared and make sure that it really works. Here a dummy means something that looks real but is not.
explain: «Kids everywhere call each other names, and the same word can be a joke or a punch.» Words can change their feeling too. A dummy said laughing between friends is teasing, but said angrily it hurts. Always check the clues.
fact: Dummy is a word with several meanings, so check the context before you choose.
fact: A dummy can be a model of a person, such as a shop dummy or a crash-test dummy.
fact: In the UK, Australia and Ireland, a dummy is a rubber teat that a baby sucks to calm down; Americans call it a pacifier.
fact: A dummy can also be something that looks real but is not, like «a dummy pill», and «a dummy run» is a practice.
fact: In some sports, a dummy is a pretend move to trick another player. A dummy is also a rude word for a silly person.
exercise: «Crash-test dummies full of sensors ride in new cars that are crashed on purpose.» In this sentence, what is a dummy? | A rude word for a silly person | *A model of a person, used to test safety | A rubber teat that a baby sucks | A pretend move in a game
exercise: In the UK, Australia and Ireland, what is a baby's dummy? | A practice run before a race | A pretend move to trick a player | A model used in shops | *A rubber teat that a baby sucks to calm down
exercise: «A placebo is a dummy treatment with no active medicine.» What does dummy mean here? | *Something that looks real but is not | A model of a person in a shop | A practice run | A rude word for a silly person
test: «The footballer sold the defender a dummy and ran past him.» What is a dummy in this sport? | A model of a person in a shop | A rubber teat for a baby | A rude word for a silly person | *A pretend move to trick another player
test: What does «a dummy run» mean? | A rude word for a silly person | *A practice, done before the real thing | A shop model that shows clothes | A rubber teat that a baby sucks
exam: A friend laughs and calls you a dummy, and both of you are grinning. What does dummy mean here? | A rubber teat for a baby | A model used in a shop | *Teasing between friends, meant as a joke | A pretend move in a game
